# NRG Bloom 301 Redirects
# Old site structure -> New site structure
#
# NOTE ON SHADOWING: Netlify serves a matching static file BEFORE it
# evaluates a non-forced redirect rule. A rule whose source path has a
# corresponding .html file in this repo will never fire unless it is
# forced with "301!". Before adding a rule here, check whether
# <source>.html exists. If it does, either delete the file or force the
# rule. This is why /team and /partnership sat at 200 for months despite
# having rules below.

/energy              /strategy           301
/impact/problem-flared-gas-nigeria      /esg-impact    301
/impact/electricity-opportunity-nigeria  /esg-impact    301
/impact/bitcoin-mining                  /strategy      301
/team                /about-leadership   301
/faq                 /investor-relations 301
/about               /about-leadership   301
/for-investors       /investor-relations 301
/blog                /insights           301
/index.html          /                   301!

# Legacy Webflow bio URLs. Confirmed 404 on 2026-08-06 while Search
# Console showed Google still sending clicks to them over the prior six
# months (/team/makir-volcy 9 clicks, /team/jordane-volcy 3 clicks).
# Specific rules first, then a catch-all for any other /team/ child.
/team/makir-volcy    /makir-volcy        301
/team/julie-peeters  /julie-peeters      301
/team/jordane-volcy  /jordane-volcy      301
/team/gus-anyim      /gus-anyim          301
/team/*              /about-leadership   301

